Pad6 - files manager for the Roland P-6
https://github.com/HomoHabilis/Pad6

Pad6 is a modified version of PyP6 by Brian Siemund,
https://github.com/j0kerpack/Roland-P6-sample-manager
The original author licensed PyP6 under the MIT License on 2026-09-30
(upstream commit 6cbbadc), as agreed in
https://github.com/j0kerpack/Roland-P6-sample-manager/discussions/2
Pad6 forked from PyP6 4.2.3, the same code that license covers. Releases of
Pad6 published before this change shipped a LICENSE that described PyP6 as
unlicensed and kept all rights on the changes; that file is superseded by
this one, and the whole project - the original code and everything changed
or added since, including the Android app in android/ - is under the MIT
License above.

The libraries and programs the downloads bundle (ffmpeg, Python and its
packages, AndroidX and Kotlin libraries, ...) are not covered by this file.
Each keeps its own license; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Pad6 writes to the storage of a Roland P-6; keep backups of anything on the
device you care about.

Roland, AIRA and P-6 are trademarks of Roland Corporation. This project is
independent and not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by Roland.
